  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic and social development with a gender perspective through text</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to improve the link between the textile practice of Yucatan and the social, economic, environmental and cultural conditions of the communities where women, families and artisan cooperatives live. All this through training for the formulation of local business models and financial education, as well as the establishment of dialogues for intercultural planning that promotes the safeguarding of living heritage linked to textile practice and the development of cultural expressions, with a focus on gender and implementation of specific indicators that contribute to the systematization and replication of the experience.</narrative>
  </description>
